{
 "deepseek": "Partially supported; major revisions required. E006c point estimates support block-25 non-necessity and head-0 involvement in the IT checkpoint, but the subject-cluster CIs are invalid due to a bootstrap deduplication bug, several per-layer/head/base claims lack provided evidence, and causal wording overstates what mean/zero ablations show. E009 has a plausible-set truncation bug and AUROC tie-handling issue. Do not cite K-0007 as established until the bootstrap is fixed, missing raw results are provided, and the wording is softened.",
 "minimax": "The narrow IT result is reasonably supported by the supplied E006c artifacts: substituting or replacing block-25 attention can strongly change a normalized answer-token logit margin, head 0 is the strongest tested head in the pooled sample, and zeroing block 25 does not reduce that margin. However, the evidence does not justify broad claims that block 25 is a uniquely causal or general late-layer factual-recall mechanism, that head 0 universally dominates, or that half the effect is independent of late attention. Relation heterogeneity, an approximate bootstrap, absent original E006b ranking data, and the lack of auditable base results materially limit the claim. The supplied E009 code also has a preregistered candidate-set deviation and a major AUROC tie-handling bug. Overall verdict: partly supported for the narrow IT intervention findings; not warranted as written for the broad mechanistic, head-uniqueness, late-attention-independence, or base-replication claims."
}
